r cement with lots of clinker we  can get to low carbon concrete uh using  low carbon cement which just has a tiny  or a short amount of clinker in it and  with this simple step we can actually  reduce the carbon footprint of concrete  on average by 60  and that's not just a pipe dream because  we've actually done it so we created  this low carbon concrete made loads of  tests in laboratories to see if it's  still a feasible material and we even  moved out of laboratories into a real  construction site so not long ago in  august we actually poured our first  concrete pour like in a real  construction site it's a foundation of a  garage to show that this low carbon  concrete actually works in reality so  that's great news low carbon concrete  exists it works you might question now  okay what does machine learning have to  do with this why do you need an i.t  company and machine learning to produce  that  okay so  as i said in order to reduce the carbon  footprint we want to reduce clinker the  challenge here is that clinker actually  makes concrete robust that means if we  reduce the clinker we get less robust  concrete  so any problems or intricacies that are  already happening in the cement  are then amplified by our low carbon  concrete and the most important property  of cement is its compressive strength  that's what's making the buildings  upright so if we have quite some  fluctuations over time in this  compressive strength these fluctuations  get amplified if we use low concrete low  carbon concrete recipes so one of the  big prerequisites for low carbon  concrete to be produced at scale is that  we have a reliable and trusty cement  strength um  and that's actually hard to achieve  because measuring cement strength takes  28 days  and the way you do this is you form  actually a concrete cube with cement  a standardized amount of water and a  standardized amount of sand and then you  have to let it sit for 28 days and  harden and then you crush it like this  